       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and individual doses usually don't go above 1,000 mg. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is high.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max daily dose.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg per day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give the clinical reason. I'll enter whichever order you choose."
