     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Family visiting and wanting things settled before rounds aren't clinical reasons for a dose like this. 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and a 1,700 mg single dose is well above the usual 1,000 mg ceiling. It could cause serious harm, including lactic acidosis, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI can enter a dose within the safe range right away, for example:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n\nIf you have a clinical reason for going above the labeled maximum, the right route is pharmacy or attending review. I can enter the order with a note flagging it for that review if you'd like. Otherwise, tell me which of the doses above you want and I'll enter it now."
      }
